+# Wire format
+
+The project's current recorded decision is to use CBOR (Concise Binary Object Representation) as the wire serialisation format. The stated rationale is that CBOR handles type information better across versions: it is self-describing, which reduces the risk of deserialisation failures when schema versions diverge and supports backward and forward compatibility as data structures evolve. This decision was recorded on 2026-09-23.
